From: DuskyProjects <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: gl-be9300: enable USB mux and port power

The IPQ5332 kernel patch gives the controller both usb and usb_dwc labels
on one flat qcom,snps-dwc3 node. Use the primary usb label in the board
DTS and opt this board into the shared USB/PCIe PHY mux selection.

The board DTS already defines usb_pins with GPIO 16 configured as an
output-high USB power enable, but the USB controller did not select that
pinctrl state. Without it the DWC3/xHCI host and both root hubs probe,
while the external port receives no VBUS and cannot enumerate devices.
Attach usb_pins to the controller so the port's 5 V supply is enabled.

---
 target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/dts/ipq5332-gl-be9300.dts
@@ -2,7 +2,10 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-&usb_dwc {
+&usb {
+	pinctrl-0 = <&usb_pins>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	qcom,multiplexed-phy;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
